# sha256 of the KernelSU-Next files this fix set patches, taken AT THE POINT
# THE BUILDER CHECKS THEM -- after the NoMount _hook/cloak stack and the
# apk-scan fix, immediately before 10_enable_susfs_for_ksu.patch.
#
# NOT a pristine 'git clone'. Baselining from upstream makes the check warn on
# EVERY build (kernel/Kbuild and feature/selinux_hide.c are rewritten by the
# NoMount stack via git apply, which prints no 'patching file' line), and a
# warning that always fires is worse than no warning. This is also the correct
# key: what decides whether the fix patches apply is the tree the enable patch
# actually sees.
#
# The set is keyed on the susfs enable patch (enable_patch.sha256); this is the
# second key. A mismatch is a WARNING -- it only matters if the matching fix
# patch then fails, and the builder quotes it back there by name.
#
# RE-CAPTURED 2026-11-16 after kernel_patches@833de46. The first capture
# (run 43750141986) predated c08306e/833de46, which moved the setprocattr probe
# from before 10_enable_susfs_for_ksu.patch to after it -- so the old
# selinux_hide.c sum was of a file that still carried the +57-line probe and
# warned on every build with no upstream move behind it. The enable patch now
# reduces selinux_hide.c cleanly: 8 rejects, not 9, and fix_selinux_hide.c.patch
# goes unused on this pair.
#
# captured from run 43922322163 (builder ce9bb516), all 8 fix patches applied,
# build green:
#   KSU          7ccf61479621f240c0d968ef46f1b167b6ceb500 (dev)
#   susfs        9b0b13f069673b9b07b713a5c66977de4d62b175 (gki-android16-6.12, v2.4.0)
#   nomount_ref  main @ 6e5560dcbd494b23d5f118a1326d304429e792ae (NMVER 1.36.0)
#   patches_ref  main
# rules.c re-captured from run 44997845922 (KSU 32e25d58fc1a187e1abe7278904c31571235fc83,
# dev moved it 3 lines; fix_rules.c.patch applied, build green).
# Refresh from the block the builder prints on mismatch -- never from upstream.
